  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">CAPABLE AND FUNCTIONAL ELEPHANTS: A CAPABILITIES APPROACH FOR MITIGATING HUMAN-ELEPHANT CONFLICT IN THE BRAHMAGIRI-NILGIRI-EASTERN GHATS LANDSCAPE OF SOUTHERN INDIA</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">THE GOAL OF THIS PROJECT IS TO DEVELOP A LANDSCAPE-LEVEL PLAN FOR THE MITIGATION OF HUMAN-ELEPHANT CONFLICT (HEC) THAT IS BASED ON AN ASSESSMENT OF CAPABILITIES AND FUNCTIONINGS OF AGRICULTURISTS AND ELEPHANTS IN THE BRAHMAGIRI-NILGIRI-EASTERN GHATS LANDSCAPE (BNEGL) OF SOUTHERN INDIA. PROJECT OBJECTIVES ARE TO: (1) MAP THE CURRENT SET OF BASIC CAPABILITIES AND FUNCTIONINGS OF AGRICULTURISTS AND ELEPHANTS (2) MODEL FUTURE SETS OF BASIC CAPABILITIES AND FUNCTIONINGS OF AGRICULTURISTS AND ELEPHANTS (3) IDENTIFY CURRENT AND FUTURE SETS OF UNREALIZED FUNCTIONING OF AGRICULTURISTS AND ELEPHANTS DUE TO HEC (4) IDENTIFY APPROPRIATE HEC MEASURES THAT MINIMIZE UNREALIZED FUNCTIONING OF AGRICULTURISTS AND ELEPHANTS AND (5) BUILD CAPACITY AND DISSEMINATE INFORMATION. PROJECT ACTIVITIES ARE TO: (1) USE VILLAGE-LEVEL CENSUS DATA, LAND-USE LAND-COVER (LULC) MODELING, QUESTIONNAIRES, SURVEYS, FOCAL GROUP DISCUSSIONS, AND MAPPING TO ASSESS THE CAPABILITY OF AGRICULTURISTS TO ACHIEVE BASIC FUNCTIONINGS (2) ANALYZE EXISTING LITERATURE ON ELEPHANT ABUNDANCE, DENSITY ESTIMATES AND DEMOGRAPHY AT THE RANGE DIVISION LEVEL, MODEL THEIR MOVEMENT USING NETLOGO AND ASSESS ELEPHANT ABUNDANCE AND DEMOGRAPHY IN SELECT ELEPHANT HABITATS TO DERIVE THE SET OF CAPABILITIES THAT AID ATTAINMENT OF THEIR BASIC FUNCTIONINGS (3) DERIVE THE BASI</narrative>
  </description>
